GEOLOCATION
================================================================

MaxMind GeoLite2
   Country lookups use the MaxMind GeoLite2-Country database and the
   com.maxmind.geoip2 reader, bound reflectively and only when present.
   This product includes GeoLite2 data created by MaxMind, available from
   https://www.maxmind.com
   When the database is absent, Verité downloads it from the license-free
   daily-refreshed mirror maintained by P3TERX.
   https://github.com/P3TERX/GeoLite.mmdb


================================================================
EXTERNAL SERVICES & REFERENCE DATA
================================================================

Mojang API
   The public, unauthenticated username-to-UUID endpoint is used as a
   last-resort resolver for names Verité has never seen locally (the /whois
   lookup). No API key is used. Minecraft and the Mojang API are the
   property of Mojang Studios / Microsoft.
   https://api.mojang.com

Minecraft protocol version table
   The mapping from a client's numeric protocol version to a human release
   name uses the wire values published on the Minecraft Wiki.
   https://minecraft.wiki/w/Protocol_version

TCPShield / proxy real-IP handshake
   Verité reads the true client IP from the proxy-injected handshake
   hostname format used by TCPShield-style anti-DDoS proxies. This is
   interoperation with a documented handshake convention, not a code
   dependency. TCPShield is the property of its respective owner.


